01:34:53.600 --> 01:34:55.397
what are we gonna do?

1549
01:35:01.000 --> 01:35:03.560
I don't fucking
believe this. Hmm?

1550
01:35:04.600 --> 01:35:07.876
This is the FBI!

1551
01:35:08.000 --> 01:35:10.309
Step away from your desks!

1552
01:35:10.440 --> 01:35:13.352
Take two big steps
away from your desks!

1553
01:35:13.480 --> 01:35:15.436
Do not touch anything!

1554
01:35:31.160 --> 01:35:34.436
How much money
was lost in the fraud,

1555
01:35:34.560 --> 01:35:36.391
- that we know of?
- Oh, billions.

1556
01:35:36.520 --> 01:35:37.873
Large institutional investors

1557
01:35:38.040 --> 01:35:39.917
- lost billions of dollars.
- So one

1558
01:35:40.040 --> 01:35:41.519
or maybe both of them,

1559
01:35:41.640 --> 01:35:45.952
two outsiders, took everybody
on Wall Street for a ride?

1560
01:35:46.080 --> 01:35:47.496
Yeah, it really looks
like they did.

1561
01:35:47.520 --> 01:35:49.750
- Yeah.
- And Acosta has vanished?

1562
01:35:49.880 --> 01:35:52.474
With hundreds of millions
of dollars.

1563
01:35:52.640 --> 01:35:55.996
Kenny Wells has always
maintained his innocence,

1564
01:35:56.120 --> 01:35:58.759
that he was duped
along with everyone else.

1565
01:35:58.880 --> 01:36:01.599
Given that,
what do you make of this?

1566
01:36:03.080 --> 01:36:07.835
Kenny Wells,
a fool or a mastermind?

1567
01:36:09.720 --> 01:36:12.075
It's a very good
question, Roger.

1568
01:36:32.360 --> 01:36:33.759
Um...

1569
01:36:36.120 --> 01:36:40.398
Mike-Mike Acosta was my friend
and, uh, my partner.

1570
01:36:40.560 --> 01:36:41.879
Um...

1571
01:36:43.160 --> 01:36:45.993
...and he-he betrayed me.

1572
01:36:46.120 --> 01:36:49.669
I-I know as CEO
of Washoe Mining

1573
01:36:49.800 --> 01:36:51.916
it's my responsibility to know

1574
01:36:52.040 --> 01:36:54.918
everything that's going on,
and I... I didn't.

1575
01:36:56.200 --> 01:36:58.395
It's not an excuse.

1576
01:36:58.520 --> 01:37:00.397
All right?
I sincerely apologize

1577
01:37:00.520 --> 01:37:04.149
to everybody and anybody
that lost on their investments.

1578
01:37:07.360 --> 01:37:09.920
Come on, Mike.

1579
01:37:10.040 --> 01:37:12.031
Mikey, come on in, man.

1580
01:37:12.160 --> 01:37:14.879
All right?

1581
01:37:15.000 --> 01:37:16.638
What happened, huh?

1582
01:37:33.920 --> 01:37:36.115
- Howard.
- I saw you on TV.

1583
01:37:36.240 --> 01:37:39.152
- Hey, man, can I talk to you for a minute, please?
- No.

1584
01:37:39.280 --> 01:37:41.157
Look, I just want to know
where my money went.

1585
01:37:41.280 --> 01:37:43.336
- Come on! - Don't know anything about it, okay?
- Mr. Wells,

1586
01:37:43.360 --> 01:37:46.193
Mr. Wells, exactly when
will you be departing?

1587
01:37:46.320 --> 01:37:49.153
Uh, later. A few days or so.
I'll let you know.

1588
01:37:49.280 --> 01:37:52.033
- We just need to talk about your bill, sir.
- I'll be down.

1589
01:37:52.160 --> 01:37:53.513
We'll settle it up.

1590
01:38:58.760 --> 01:39:00.830
Do I need a lawyer?

1591
01:39:00.960 --> 01:39:03.394
Do you need a lawyer?

1592
01:39:06.760 --> 01:39:08.671
Right answer.

1593
01:39:20.720 --> 01:39:22.676
How'd you meet Michael Acosta?

1594
01:39:26.000 --> 01:39:29.231
The, uh, first time
or the second time?

1595
01:39:29.400 --> 01:39:31.755
How'd you meet him, Wells?

1596
01:39:33.720 --> 01:39:36.632
It was April... of '88.

1597
01:39:38.520 --> 01:39:40.715
Yeah, I was
on the balls of my ass.

1598
01:39:40.840 --> 01:39:43.513
Scrambling.

1599
01:39:43.640 --> 01:39:46.791
Not exactly uncharted waters
for me, but...

1600
01:39:46.920 --> 01:39:49.275
I was in deep.

1601
01:39:57.360 --> 01:39:58.998
I think it's pretty unlikely

1602
01:39:59.120 --> 01:40:01.111
we'll ever see
your partner again.

1603
01:40:03.680 --> 01:40:06.148
- What are you talking about?
- A lot of very powerful people

1604
01:40:06.280 --> 01:40:08.191
are very angry
at Michael Acosta.

1605
01:40:12.200 --> 01:40:13.679
Well, what happened?

1606
01:40:13.800 --> 01:40:14.869
What happened?

1607
01:40:15.000 --> 01:40:17.673
$17 billion of value
disappeared overnight.

1608
01:40:17.800 --> 01:40:19.080
Mike Acosta
waves good-bye to you

1609
01:40:19.240 --> 01:40:21.320
in the ballroom downstairs
and goes back to lndonesia

1610
01:40:21.440 --> 01:40:23.829
on a jet chartered
with Washoe funds.

1611
01:40:23.960 --> 01:40:26.713
And then he does
a disappearing act.

1612
01:40:26.840 --> 01:40:28.876
But this you know.

1613
01:40:29.040 --> 01:40:32.396
First, he's locked out
of the assay lab in Kalimantan

1614
01:40:32.520 --> 01:40:34.909
by the minister
of the interior.

1615
01:40:35.040 --> 01:40:36.837
- So he goes back to Jakarta...
- Mr. Acosta,

1616
01:40:36.960 --> 01:40:38.359
please walk with with me.

1617
01:40:38.480 --> 01:40:40.357
...where he's
immediately detained

1618
01:40:40.480 --> 01:40:42.436
by the Indonesian military.

1619
01:40:44.080 --> 01:40:45.433
And they hold him

1620
01:40:45.600 --> 01:40:47.670
while they try to reproduce
for themselves

1621
01:40:47.800 --> 01:40:50.109
the lab results claimed
by Washoe.

1622
01:40:51.760 --> 01:40:54.593
Which, of course,
they are unable to do.

1623
01:40:54.720 --> 01:40:57.359
Now, at this point,

1624
01:40:57.480 --> 01:41:00.472
either he's being transferred
to an actual prison, or...

1625
01:41:00.600 --> 01:41:02.397
he's bribed
one of the officers.

1626
01:41:02.520 --> 01:41:03.555
Either way,

1627
01:41:03.680 --> 01:41:05.272
he's on a military helicopter.

1628
01:41:07.080 --> 01:41:10.152
They fly north, loosely
tracking the Kensana River.

1629
01:41:57.680 --> 01:42:01.798
A thousand feet up,
over the Kensana...

1630
01:42:01.920 --> 01:42:04.480
Mike Acosta takes a header.

1631
01:42:15.040 --> 01:42:17.793
No way.

1632
01:42:17.920 --> 01:42:20.593
No fucking way.

1633
01:42:20.720 --> 01:42:22.517
He either faked it,

1634
01:42:22.640 --> 01:42:24.790
or he paid to have
this-this bullshit story

1635
01:42:24.920 --> 01:42:26.433
you're telling put out.

1636
01:42:26.560 --> 01:42:30.792
$164 million goes a long way
in lndonesia.

1637
01:42:30.920 --> 01:42:33.434
They found a body.

1638
01:42:48.840 --> 01:42:51.229
Hands and face were eaten away,

1639
01:42:51.360 --> 01:42:54.272
probably by wild pigs.

1640
01:42:54.400 --> 01:42:56.960
Sure this is him?

1641
01:42:57.080 --> 01:42:59.389
I'm not sure of anything...

1642
01:42:59.520 --> 01:43:04.196
except Mike Acosta traded
water filters for river gold.

1643
01:43:04.360 --> 01:43:05.918
But now
the Indonesian government

1644
01:43:06.040 --> 01:43:07.314
have gone unusually quiet

1645
01:43:07.440 --> 01:43:09.078
on the subject.

1646
01:43:09.240 --> 01:43:10.832
There was an autopsy

1647
01:43:10.960 --> 01:43:12.951
corroborating the identity
of the body.

1648
01:43:14.280 --> 01:43:16.840
They then sealed the report...

1649
01:43:18.560 --> 01:43:20.596
...cremated the remains.

1650
01:43:20.720 --> 01:43:25.157
Interestingly,
Danny Suharto, your friend...

1651
01:43:25.280 --> 01:43:28.158
dumped a lot of stock as well.

1652
01:43:28.280 --> 01:43:31.113
So the Suhartos
are even richer now.

1653
01:43:31.240 --> 01:43:34.550
Mike Acosta is ostensibly
dead and buried, and...

1654
01:43:34.680 --> 01:43:36.989
$164 million is still missing.

1655
01:43:37.120 --> 01:43:40.476
And the only question...

1656
01:43:40.600 --> 01:43:42.795
I'm left with is...

1657
01:43:42.920 --> 01:43:45.434
whether or not
you were in on it.

1658
01:43:47.560 --> 01:43:49.790
I...

1659
01:43:49.920 --> 01:43:53.230
- I can't believe it.
- Can't believe what?

1660
01:43:53.360 --> 01:43:56.909
No, look, th-this business...

1661
01:43:57.080 --> 01:43:59.640
had written Mike off
years ago, all right?

1662
01:43:59.760 --> 01:44:01.159
They called his theories crap.

1663
01:44:01.280 --> 01:44:03.191
But...

1664
01:44:03.320 --> 01:44:05.151
there's no way.

1665
01:44:05.280 --> 01:44:07.191
He wouldn't,
he fucking couldn't

1666
01:44:07.320 --> 01:44:09.436
let this be
the last word on him.

1667
01:44:09.560 --> 01:44:13.155
- No fucking way.
- You talking about Acosta or yourself?

1668
01:44:23.000 --> 01:44:26.515
All right, look. We-we-we were
running out of money, right?

1669
01:44:26.640 --> 01:44:29.154
And I was practically dying
from malaria.

1670
01:44:29.320 --> 01:44:31.959
I gave Mike
the last dollar to my name.

1671
01:44:32.080 --> 01:44:34.753
And I made him promise me
something, I said, "Mike...

1672
01:44:34.880 --> 01:44:38.316
don't let me die out here
for nothing."

1673
01:44:43.320 --> 01:44:46.312
A few weeks later,
I came to, and...

1674
01:44:46.440 --> 01:44:48.396
Mike was there.

1675
01:44:52.000 --> 01:44:54.070
He said, "We got...

1676
01:44:54.200 --> 01:44:56.350
"we got a strike, Kenny.

1677
01:44:57.640 --> 01:44:59.995
We got a goddamn gold mine."

1678
01:45:04.520 --> 01:45:09.435
And th-there's no way that
he set out to swindle anyone.

1679
01:45:09.560 --> 01:45:12.199
He just needed
to buy a little more time.

1680
01:45:17.320 --> 01:45:19.356
And he didn't want
to let me down.

1681
01:45:19.480 --> 01:45:23.314
- You're fuckin' lyin'.
- Levine, sit down!

1682
01:45:23.440 --> 01:45:25.192
You want to talk
about the truth?

1683
01:45:25.320 --> 01:45:26.878
All right,
let's talk about the truth.

1684
01:45:27.000 --> 01:45:29.150
The only truth here is,
when everybody's getting rich,

1685
01:45:29.280 --> 01:45:32.078
nobody gives a shit
about the truth.

1686
01:45:32.200 --> 01:45:35.272
Come the fuck on.
All anyone had to do was look,

1687
01:45:35.400 --> 01:45:37.118
open their eyes.

1688
01:45:37.240 --> 01:45:40.312
Man, the-the gold was wrong,
the find was too good.

1689
01:45:40.440 --> 01:45:43.000
There were red flags
everywhere.

1690
01:45:43.120 --> 01:45:44.758
Why did no one look?

1691
01:45:44.880 --> 01:45:46.836
'Cause no one wanted
to fucking know.

1692
01:45:46.960 --> 01:45:48.837
We all wanted to believe.

1693
01:45:48.960 --> 01:45:50.871
Me, you,
fucking everybody. Why?

1694
01:45:52.360 --> 01:45:55.636
Because we were all making
so much fucking money, man.

1695
01:45:55.760 --> 01:45:57.990
That's the truth.

1696
01:45:58.160 --> 01:46:00.833
That's been going on
for fucking centuries!

1697
01:46:02.520 --> 01:46:05.671
Oh, fuck...

1698
01:46:08.720 --> 01:46:11.280
Were you aware Mike Acosta
was salting

1699
01:46:11.400 --> 01:46:13.789
- the Washoe core samples?
- No.

1700
01:46:13.920 --> 01:46:15.353
You had no knowledge

1701
01:46:15.480 --> 01:46:18.313
Mike Acosta
was perpetrating a fraud?

1702
01:46:18.440 --> 01:46:20.795
- No.
- You were not in collusion

1703
01:46:20.920 --> 01:46:23.798
with Mike Acosta
on the Kensana gold strike?

1704
01:46:23.920 --> 01:46:27.833
No, man, I fucking thought
I won the lottery.

1705
01:46:27.960 --> 01:46:31.350
Did you profit
from the Kensana fraud?

1706
01:46:33.680 --> 01:46:36.114
- No.
- Did anyone close to you profit?

1707
01:46:37.840 --> 01:46:40.400
My friends lost money.

1708
01:46:40.520 --> 01:46:42.397
My neighbors lost money.

1709
01:46:42.520 --> 01:46:44.556
Me...

1710
01:46:44.680 --> 01:46:47.240
I lost everything.

1711
01:46:50.120 --> 01:46:52.588
You know
what the truth of it is?

1712
01:46:54.040 --> 01:46:56.190
I never really cared
about money.

1713
01:46:57.280 --> 01:46:59.794
I cared about gold.

1714
01:46:59.920 --> 01:47:02.115
And it's different, Jennings.

1715
01:47:02.240 --> 01:47:04.276
It's fucking different.

1716
01:47:23.320 --> 01:47:26.676
Interview terminated
with Kenny Wells...

1717
01:47:26.800 --> 01:47:29.712
6:45 a.m.,

1718
01:47:29.880 --> 01:47:33.395
October 17, 1988.

1719
01:47:33.520 --> 01:47:34.794
Interview conducted by myself,

1720
01:47:34.920 --> 01:47:37.115
Paul K. Jennings,
special agent.

1721
01:47:37.240 --> 01:47:40.391
Also present,
agents Levine and Banks,

1722
01:47:40.520 --> 01:47:42.397
Federal Bureau of lnvestigation,

1723
01:47:42.520 --> 01:47:44.317
district of Nevada, Reno.

1724
01:47:56.600 --> 01:47:58.716
Mr. Kenny Wells...

1725
01:48:01.640 --> 01:48:03.915
...you are free to go.

1726
01:48:05.600 --> 01:48:08.478
Well, lookee there.

1727
01:48:08.600 --> 01:48:10.830
Somebody believes me.

1728
01:48:12.640 --> 01:48:14.949
I wouldn't go overboard.

1729
01:48:15.080 --> 01:48:18.550
In fact,
I wouldn't leave the state,

1730
01:48:18.720 --> 01:48:21.314
or start buying new stuff
or chartering

1731
01:48:21.440 --> 01:48:23.016
- any more jets.
- I gotta sneak by the guy

1732
01:48:23.040 --> 01:48:24.896
at the front desk 'cause
I can't pay the hotel bill.

1733
01:48:24.920 --> 01:48:27.798
I can't be a party
to that information.

1734
01:48:28.880 --> 01:48:31.155
Good luck, Mr. Wells.

1735
01:48:31.280 --> 01:48:34.238
We'll be keeping an eye on you.

1736
01:48:39.760 --> 01:48:42.069
What are you gonna do now,
Wells?

1737
01:50:03.320 --> 01:50:04.833
Hey, Kenny.

1738
01:50:04.960 --> 01:50:06.480
I-I'm still worried
about that mulberry

1739
01:50:06.560 --> 01:50:08.949
- over the back fence.
- Yeah. I know, Hart.

1740
01:50:09.120 --> 01:50:10.792
It's good to see you.

1741
01:50:10.920 --> 01:50:12.797
Good to see you, too, Kenny.

1742
01:50:43.480 --> 01:50:45.550
Can I come in?

1743
01:51:21.520 --> 01:51:24.034
- You want coffee?
- Yeah, sure.

1744
01:51:29.920 --> 01:51:32.195
This place looks great.

1745
01:51:35.800 --> 01:51:37.995
So do you, Kay.

1746
01:51:42.680 --> 01:51:44.318
I made curtains.

1747
01:51:44.440 --> 01:51:47.034
From that fabric.

1748
01:51:47.160 --> 01:51:48.479
Hmm.

1749
01:51:51.720 --> 01:51:54.314
Some stuff came for you,
some mail.

1750
01:52:43.400 --> 01:52:44.799
What?

1751
01:52:44.920 --> 01:52:47.514
What is it?
